📚 OVERVIEW:
This is a carefully structured progression of 20 basic Linked List problems 
designed to build your understanding from absolute basics to practical 
applications in Java. Each problem introduces one new concept at a time.

🎯 LEARNING PHILOSOPHY:
- Start with the absolute basics (what is a node?)
- Build concepts incrementally (create → traverse → modify)
- Practice with simple, clear problems
- Focus on Singly Linked Lists first
- End with common interview patterns

🗂️ PROBLEM CATEGORIES:
Phase 1: Foundation (Problems 1-4) - Understanding nodes and basic structure
Phase 2: Creation & Display (Problems 5-7) - Building and printing lists
Phase 3: Insertion Mastery (Problems 8-11) - Adding elements everywhere
Phase 4: Deletion Skills (Problems 12-14) - Removing elements safely
Phase 5: Search & Access (Problems 15-16) - Finding and retrieving data
Phase 6: Advanced Operations (Problems 17-20) - Reverse, cycle, and patterns

