🐛 COMMON DEBUGGING TIPS
===============================================================================

🔍 **Debugging Checklist:**
□ **Null Pointer Exceptions**: Always check if node != null before accessing
□ **Infinite Loops**: Ensure pointers are updated in each iteration
□ **Head Updates**: Remember to update head when adding/removing first element
□ **Memory Leaks**: In languages with manual memory management (not Java)
□ **Edge Cases**: Test with empty list, single element, and two elements

🔍 **Print Debugging Template:**
```java
public void debugPrint(String operation) {
    System.out.println("After " + operation + ":");
    display();
    System.out.println("Head points to: " + (head != null ? head.data : "null"));
    System.out.println("Size: " + size());
    System.out.println("---");
}
```

